#: ../../../CommandGuide/lit.md:690
msgid "TEST RUN OUTPUT FORMAT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/lit.md:692
msgid ""
"The {program}`lit` output for a test run conforms to the following schema, "
"in both short and verbose modes (although in short mode no PASS lines will "
"be shown). This schema has been chosen to be relatively easy to reliably "
"parse by a machine (for example in buildbot log scraping), and for other "
"tools to generate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/lit.md:698
msgid "Each test result is expected to appear on a line that matches:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/lit.md:704
msgid ""
"where `<result-code>` is a standard test result such as PASS, FAIL, XFAIL, "
"XPASS, UNRESOLVED, or UNSUPPORTED. The performance result codes of IMPROVED "
"and REGRESSED are also allowed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/lit.md:708
msgid ""
"The `<test name>` field can consist of an arbitrary string containing no "
"newline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/lit.md:711
msgid ""
"The `<progress info>` field can be used to report progress information such "
"as (1/300) or can be empty, but even when empty the parentheses are required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/lit.md:714
msgid ""
"Should a test be allowed retries (see `ALLOW_RETRIES:` annotation) and it "
"needed more than one attempt to succeed, then `<progress info>` is extended "
"by this information:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/lit.md:722
msgid ""
"Each test result may include additional (multiline) log information in the "
"following format:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/lit.md:731
msgid ""
"where `<test name>` should be the name of a preceding reported test, `<log "
"delineator>` is a string of \"\\*\" characters *at least* four characters "
"long (the recommended length is 20), and `<trailing delineator>` is an "
"arbitrary (unparsed) string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/lit.md:736
msgid ""
"The following is an example of a test run output which consists of four "
"tests A, B, C, and D, and a log message for the failing test C:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/lit.md:749
msgid "DEFAULT FEATURES"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/lit.md:751
msgid ""
"For convenience {program}`lit` automatically adds **available_features** for "
"some common use cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/lit.md:754
msgid ""
"{program}`lit` adds a feature based on the operating system being built on, "
"for example: `system-darwin`, `system-linux`, etc. {program}`lit` also "
"automatically adds a feature based on the current architecture, for example "
"`target-x86_64`, `target-aarch64`, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/lit.md:759
msgid ""
"When building with sanitizers enabled, {program}`lit` automatically adds the "
"short name of the sanitizer, for example: `asan`, `tsan`, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/lit.md:762
msgid ""
"To see the full list of features that can be added, see *llvm/utils/lit/lit/"
"llvm/config.py*."
msgstr ""

